// QuicBaaS FIDO2 / WebAuthn Ceremony Protocol Buffer Definitions v1
//
// The FIDO2 ceremony surface (quicbaas.FIDO2) is the go-xkms FIDO2 transport
// contract verbatim: BeginRegistration / FinishRegistration /
// BeginAuthentication / FinishAuthentication exchanging opaque WebAuthn
// ceremony JSON (options_json / attestation_json / assertion_json) plus an
// opaque session id. The only QuicBaaS addition is the explicit tenant_id on
// each request, because QuicBaaS runs one relying-party service per tenant
// while xkms runs exactly one. The server delegates to the tenant-scoped
// FIDO2 composition service (pkg/service FIDO2Service), which wraps the
// per-tenant xkms relying-party service in go-xkms's canonical FIDO2
// servicer adapter.
//
// SECURITY: the authentication verbs (BeginAuthentication /
// FinishAuthentication) are pre-auth — WebAuthn IS the authentication
// mechanism, matching the public posture of the REST
// /api/v1/iam/{tenant}/webauthn/login/* routes. The registration verbs bind
// a new authenticator to a user and are authz-gated (user_authfactors:add),
// matching /api/v1/iam/{tenant}/webauthn/registration/*.
